1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,490
Three in the morning.

2
00:00:02,140 --> 00:00:04,010
Your Hyperliquid position is minutes

3
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:05,030
from liquidation,

4
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:06,070
and you're asleep.

5
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:09,330
It happens to traders every day.

6
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:11,490
In one October cascade,

7
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:13,840
over seven point four billion dollars

8
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:16,830
of Hyperliquid positions were wiped out.

9
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:18,990
Lifeline,

10
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:20,150
built on NEAR,

11
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,150
stops that.

12
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:24,030
It watches your account every five seconds,

13
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:25,950
and tops up your margin from

14
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:27,490
a reserve you fund from any

15
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:28,930
chain through NEAR Intents.

16
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:32,550
NEAR Intents swaps your funds from

17
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,950
any chain into USDC on NEAR,

18
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:36,750
and you deposit it into the

19
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:37,450
Lifeline vault.

20
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:40,270
Then set your rules:

21
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:41,690
when to warn you,

22
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:42,630
when to rescue,

23
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:43,890
and how much.

24
00:00:45,340 --> 00:00:47,130
The keeper reads your health every

25
00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:47,890
five seconds.

26
00:00:48,460 --> 00:00:49,130
At one,

27
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:50,210
you're liquidated.

28
00:00:51,460 --> 00:00:52,470
Below your trigger,

29
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:54,810
it gets a signed quote from 1Click,

30
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:56,610
and the vault pays it straight

31
00:00:56,460 --> 00:00:58,170
into your Hyperliquid margin.

32
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:00,610
On testnet,

33
00:01:00,860 --> 00:01:03,030
that money reached Hyperliquid in under

34
00:01:02,880 --> 00:01:04,090
fifteen seconds.

35
00:01:05,340 --> 00:01:06,750
You wake up to a message

36
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:07,690
explaining it.

37
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:09,830
Every step is on a public ledger.

38
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,770
A bot that moves money is

39
00:01:12,620 --> 00:01:13,290
a target.

40
00:01:13,580 --> 00:01:15,670
So we assume it gets hacked.

41
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:18,250
On the attack page,

42
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:20,290
anyone can play a hacked keeper

43
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:21,390
holding the real key.

44
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:23,110
It tries to pay itself.

45
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:25,650
The vault refuses,

46
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:26,590
on chain.

47
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:28,970
The key can only call rescue,

48
00:01:29,240 --> 00:01:31,270
and the vault checks every quote itself.

49
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:34,090
Edit a signed quote.

50
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:35,910
Take more than the cap.

51
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:37,570
Replay an old one.

52
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:38,830
Seven tricks,

53
00:01:39,260 --> 00:01:40,310
seven refusals.

54
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:42,670
Don't trust us:

55
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:45,090
the verify page checks every claim

56
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:45,770
in your browser,

57
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:48,510
even each AI explanation's signature.

58
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:50,730
Under the hood:

59
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:52,850
a sixteen-rule policy engine,

60
00:01:53,260 --> 00:01:54,710
a Rust vault on NEAR,

61
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:56,570
NEAR Intents for the money,

62
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,610
and NEAR AI for the words.

63
00:02:00,240 --> 00:02:02,630
On eighteen thousand replayed positions,

64
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:04,950
thirty-four percent were liquidated

65
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:05,890
without protection.

66
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:07,290
With Lifeline,

67
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:09,755
twenty point six.

68
00:02:09,605 --> 00:02:10,970
Three in the morning.

69
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:12,170
You're asleep.

70
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:14,230
And your position is still open.

